// IMAGE: the displayed value of an El-term, through υᴰ, is the
// section's image of its value — at a binder by sec-values-ext, at a
// constructor by reflection at its point slot of ⟦Φ⟧ˢ.

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ      Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ₙ 𝒮      Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮      𝒰̄ ≼ ℓ      Γ ⊦ Φ ⊑ₛ Φ′
Γ ; Φ′ ⊦ 𝕥 : El 𝕦
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (sec-image)   // admissible, by induction on 𝕥
Γ · ⟦𝒮⟧ · ⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄ · ⟦Φ ⊑ Φ′⟧ˢ ⊦ (⟦𝕥⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[υᴰ] ≐ ⟦𝕦⟧ˢ ⟦𝕥⟧[υ][υᴰ] : (⟦𝕦⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄ ⟦𝕥⟧[υ])[υᴰ]

### Sections

// A SECTION of d̄ is a spine h̄ of the section telescope at the
// initial algebra; THE ELIMINATOR 𝒮-elim d̄ is the one the initial
// algebra has. A SLOT is its position's variable, instantiated
// (disp-lookup, sec-lookup: admissible, el-var at the slot); the
// eliminator is the spine of its slots (sp-eta).

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮      𝒰̄ ≼ ℓ      Γ ⊦ d̄ : (⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[id, ι(𝒮)]
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-qiit-elim)
Γ ⊦ 𝒮-elim d̄ : ⟦𝒮⟧ˢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄]

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮      𝒰̄ ≼ ℓ      Γ ⊦ d̄ : (⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[id, ι(𝒮)]
Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝒮‖ᵢ ≐ 𝔄 qty      𝒰̄‖ᵢ = 𝒰
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (disp-lookup) // admissible
Γ ⊦ ☐ᵢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄] : (⟦𝔄⟧ᴰ 𝒰 ⟦⬡ᵢ⟧[υ])[id, ι(𝒮), d̄]

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮      𝒰̄ ≼ ℓ      Γ ⊦ d̄ : (⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[id, ι(𝒮)]
Γ ⊦ h̄ : ⟦𝒮⟧ˢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄]      Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝒮‖ᵢ ≐ 𝔄 qty
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (sec-lookup) // admissible
Γ ⊦ ☐ᵢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄, h̄] : (⟦𝔄⟧ˢ ⟦⬡ᵢ⟧[υ][υᴰ] (⟦⬡ᵢ⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[υᴰ])[id, ι(𝒮), d̄, h̄]

## Computation

// (β) is el-reflect at a point slot: ☐ᵢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄, 𝒮-elim d̄] θ, i a
// point entry, proves, by
// sec-lookup and the clauses of _ˢ, that the sort eliminator at the
// saturated constructor is the method at the arguments and their
// induction hypotheses — the eliminator's own values (sec-image);
// reflected, it computes. EQUATION constructors have no β: their
// slots are ⋆.

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮      𝒰̄ ≼ ℓ      Γ ⊦ d̄ : (⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[id, ι(𝒮)]
Γ ; 𝒮 ⊦ 𝒮‖ᵢ ≐ 𝔄 qty      Γ ⊦ θ : ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[id, ι(𝒮)]      Γ ⊦ ☐ᵢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄, 𝒮-elim d̄] θ : (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ A)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-qiit-beta)   // admissible, el-reflect
Γ ⊦ a₀ ≐ a₁ : A

## Uniqueness

// (η) — the section is unique (initiality): two maps out of a QIIT
// that agree on all constructors are equal.

Γ ⊦ 𝒮 qctx ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝒰̄ targets 𝒮      𝒰̄ ≼ ℓ      Γ ⊦ d̄ : (⟦𝒮⟧ᴰ 𝒰̄)[id, ι(𝒮)]
Γ ⊦ h̄ : ⟦𝒮⟧ˢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄]
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-qiit-eta)
Γ ⊦ h̄ ≐ 𝒮-elim d̄ : ⟦𝒮⟧ˢ[id, ι(𝒮), d̄]

## Substitution action

// Substitution acts through the carried signature (𝒮[σ]: Nova
// substitution, Theory of signatures; the reading commutes with it,
// ⟦𝒮[σ]⟧ = ⟦𝒮⟧[σ]).

Γ₁ ⊦ 𝒮.𝕤 ē : 𝕌ℓ
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------------- (ty-sub-qiit)
Γ₀ ⊦ (𝒮.𝕤 ē)[σ] ≐ 𝒮[σ].𝕤 ē[σ] : 𝕌ℓ

Γ₁ ⊦ 𝒮.𝕔 θ : A
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------------- (el-sub-qiit-intro)
Γ₀ ⊦ (𝒮.𝕔 θ)[σ] ≐ 𝒮[σ].𝕔 θ[σ] : A[σ]

Γ₁ ⊦ 𝒮-elim d̄ : Δ
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------------------- (sp-sub-qiit-elim)
Γ₀ ⊦ (𝒮-elim d̄)[σ] ≐ 𝒮[σ]-elim d̄[σ] : Δ[σ]

## Notes

//   * SUBSUMPTION. ℕ is 𝒮.𝕟 · for 𝒮 = (𝕟 : U; Z : El 𝕟;
//     S : (𝕧 : El 𝕟) ⇛ El 𝕟). The quotient A / R is 𝒮.𝕢 · for the
//     signature under IDENTITY above. The disjoint union A ⊎ B is
//     𝒮.𝕤 · for 𝒮 = (𝕤 : U; inl : (x : A) ⇛ El 𝕤;
//     inr : (y : B) ⇛ El 𝕤) — two external-domain points, no
//     equations; its eliminator's β and η are el-qiit-beta/-eta at
//     that signature, which is exactly why ⊎'s standalone rules could
//     be READ OFF the scheme. An indexed inductive type
//     (well-founded trees included) is a sorts-and-points signature:
//     sorts with index arities over I, one point constructor per node
//     shape whose inductive binders are the subtrees. Because QIIT
//     equality is structural (IDENTITY above), these are genuine
//     equalities, not just encodings: ℕ and (/) are kept for
//     convenience but are DERIVABLE, each a one-line signature.
//     (The levels agree — ℕ's signature embeds no Nova types at all,
//     so it is at level 0, and a quotient's, A : 𝕌ℓ with R : Ω, is
//     at A's level — so ty-nat/ty-quot at every level are
//     subsumed too.)
//   * RELAXATION. Strict positivity is GRAMMATICAL — Π domains are
//     only Nova types (sort-free: the Nova zone has no inductive
//     variables) or El-codes; U and Π-types never occur left of a ⇛.
//     This grammar is the DECIDABLE proxy for a semantic condition:
//     that the signature's operator be monotone on the lattice of
//     relations (the setoid congruences over the carrier). A
//     future revision could widen the domain grammar and instead
//     discharge a monotonicity obligation as an ordinary premise,
//     admitting monotone-but-not-positive operators; postulated here
//     in the positive fragment only.
//   * SEMANTICS. The postulate asserts that 𝒮's INITIAL ALGEBRA exists
//     in the setoid model: carriers are the constructor terms, the
//     setoid relation is the congruence GENERATED by the equation
//     constructors (no quotienting step — coarsening the relation IS
//     the quotient), 𝒮-elim is the unique section into any displayed
//     algebra (el-qiit-eta), and β holds on the nose. This is the
//     initiality commitment of Altenkirch–Kaposi–Kovács (finitary QIITs),
//     transported to the proof-irrelevant setoid setting where the
//     coherence tower degenerates. As with the injectivity rules,
//     models that fail initiality are hereby excluded.

## Example

// (inductive-inductive: contexts and types). The signature
//     𝒮 = ( Con : U
//         ; Ty  : (𝕘 : El Con) ⇛ U
//         ; ⋄   : El Con
//         ; ext : (𝕘 : El Con) ⇛ (𝕒 : El (Ty 𝕘)) ⇛ El Con      # Γ ▷ A
//         ; u   : (𝕘 : El Con) ⇛ El (Ty 𝕘)
//         ; pi  : (𝕘 : El Con) ⇛ (𝕒 : El (Ty 𝕘))
//                   ⇛ (𝕓 : El (Ty (ext 𝕘 𝕒))) ⇛ El (Ty 𝕘) )
//   gives types 𝒮.Con · and 𝒮.Ty c (Ty indexed by Con); induction is
//   induction-induction — a motive for Con and one for Ty over it, the
//   methods respecting the dependency.
//
// EXAMPLE (quotient: finite multisets over an external type A).
//     𝒮 = ( Bag : U
//         ; nil : El Bag
//         ; ins : (x : A) ⇛ (𝕞 : El Bag) ⇛ El Bag              # x ∷ m
//         ; swp : (x y : A) ⇛ (𝕞 : El Bag)
//                   ⇛ El (ins x (ins y 𝕞) ≡ ins y (ins x 𝕞)) )
//   swp is an equation constructor; 𝒮.Bag ·'s eliminator carries the
//   coherence premise that the method for ins is invariant under
//   swapping the two heads — the multiset laws, no transport.

# Coinductive types (polynomial codes)
//
// The dual scheme to QIITs, in its smallest useful form: a POLYNOMIAL
// 𝔽 is a one-hole strictly positive code, no binders over the hole,
// no internal fixpoints. The polarity is Π's, not ℕ's: canonical
// forms are corec-headed, out forces lazily, and elements are
// compared by observation. Like a QIIT signature written out, 𝔽 is
// carried by the formers and compared structurally; unlike one, it
// has no Σ-entry and mints no names.
//
// THE EXTENSIONAL PAYOFF, dual to the QIIT section's: uniqueness of
// the corecursor is a plain judgemental rule. In intensional
// theories judgemental finality is rejected as undecidable, and
// coinductive equality degenerates into hand-rolled bisimulation
// setoids; here ≐ is already reflection-strong, so el-nu-eta is
// homogeneous with el-qiit-eta — and BISIMULATION IMPLIES EQUALITY
// becomes a corollary rather than a discipline.

## Polynomials

// Grammar. A left-hand type `a` BINDS a Nova variable in its body,
// exactly as ty-sigma/ty-pi bind; the two product forms are
// distinguished by their left-hand side. The hole 𝕏 never occurs left
// of a → — strict positivity is GRAMMATICAL, with nothing to check
// (the same decidable-proxy commitment as RELAXATION in the QIIT
// notes: here the semantic condition is that 𝔽's operator be monotone
// on the setoid lattice).

//   polynomial
    𝔽, 𝔾 ::= 𝕏               // the hole
           | K t             // constant at a code
           | 𝔽 × 𝔽           // product
           | 𝔽 ⊎ 𝔽           // sum — onto the native ⊎
           | t × 𝔽        // dependent pair over external data
                             //   (binds a NOVA variable)
           | t → 𝔽        // exponent with external domain
                             //   (binds a NOVA variable)

Γ ctx
--------------- (poly-hole)
Γ ⊦ 𝕏 poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌ℓ
---------------- (poly-const)
Γ ⊦ K a poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝔾 poly ℓ
---------------------------- (poly-prod)
Γ ⊦ 𝔽 × 𝔾 poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ 𝔾 poly ℓ
---------------------------- (poly-sum)
Γ ⊦ 𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾 poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌ℓ      Γ ▷ a ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ
---------------------------------- (poly-sigma)
Γ ⊦ a × 𝔽 poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌ℓ      Γ ▷ a ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ
---------------------------------- (poly-pi)
Γ ⊦ a → 𝔽 poly ℓ

// REFLECTION ⌊𝔽⌋(c): the code with the hole filled by Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ.

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
--------------------------------------- (ty-poly ℓ)
Γ ⊦ ⌊𝔽⌋(c) : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
----------------------- (ty-poly-hole)
Γ ⊦ ⌊𝕏⌋(c) ≐ c : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
--------------------------- (ty-poly-const)
Γ ⊦ ⌊K a⌋(c) ≐ a : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 × 𝔾 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
------------------------------------------------ (ty-poly-prod)   // ty-sigma, non-dependent
Γ ⊦ ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c) ≐ ⌊𝔽⌋(c) × ⌊𝔾⌋(c)[↑] : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
------------------------------------------------ (ty-poly-sum)
Γ ⊦ ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c) ≐ ⌊𝔽⌋(c) ⊎ ⌊𝔾⌋(c) : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ a × 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
------------------------------------------------ (ty-poly-sigma)
Γ ⊦ ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c) ≐ a × ⌊𝔽⌋(c[↑]) : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ a → 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ
------------------------------------------------ (ty-poly-pi)
Γ ⊦ ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c) ≐ a → ⌊𝔽⌋(c[↑]) : 𝕌ℓ

// FUNCTORIAL ACTION map_𝔽 g, a function term. The functor laws —
// map_𝔽 (λ ☐₀) ≐ λ ☐₀, and map of a composite is the composite of the
// maps, pointwise — are derivable per polynomial (β, η and ⊎-eta per
// former).

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c₀ : 𝕌ℓ      Γ ⊦ c₁ : 𝕌ℓ      Γ ⊦ g : c₀ → c₁[↑]
---------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-map)
Γ ⊦ map_𝔽 g : ⌊𝔽⌋(c₀) → ⌊𝔽⌋(c₁)[↑]

Γ ⊦ map_𝕏 g : ⌊𝕏⌋(c₀) → ⌊𝕏⌋(c₁)[↑]      Γ ⊦ x : c₀
---------------------------------------------------- (el-map-hole)
Γ ⊦ map_𝕏 g x ≐ g x : c₁

Γ ⊦ map_{K a} g : ⌊K a⌋(c₀) → ⌊K a⌋(c₁)[↑]      Γ ⊦ x : a
---------------------------------------------------------- (el-map-const)
Γ ⊦ map_{K a} g x ≐ x : a

Γ ⊦ map_{𝔽 × 𝔾} g : ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c₀) → ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c₁)[↑]      Γ ⊦ p : ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c₀)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-map-prod)
Γ ⊦ map_{𝔽 × 𝔾} g p ≐ (map_𝔽 g (p .π₁) , map_𝔾 g (p .π₂)) : ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c₁)

Γ ⊦ map_{𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾} g : ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c₀) → ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c₁)[↑]      Γ ⊦ s : ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c₀)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-map-sum)
Γ ⊦ map_{𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾} g s ≐ ⊎-elim (inj₁ ((map_𝔽 g)[↑] ☐₀)) (inj₂ ((map_𝔾 g)[↑] ☐₀)) s : ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c₁)

Γ ⊦ map_{a × 𝔽} g : ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c₀) → ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c₁)[↑]      Γ ⊦ p : ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c₀)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-map-sigma)
Γ ⊦ map_{a × 𝔽} g p ≐ (p .π₁ , map_{𝔽[id, p .π₁]} g (p .π₂)) : ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c₁)

Γ ⊦ map_{a → 𝔽} g : ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c₀) → ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c₁)[↑]      Γ ⊦ f : ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c₀)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-map-pi)
Γ ⊦ map_{a → 𝔽} g f ≐ λ (map_𝔽 g[↑] (f[↑] ☐₀)) : ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c₁)

## Identity

// (structural). ν 𝔽 carries its polynomial, compared componentwise
// and iso-recursively: the comparison never unfolds the fixpoint into
// its body. ν 𝔽 and ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽) are ISOMORPHIC (out one way; in, in the
// Notes, the other) and deliberately never ≐ — same commitment as the
// QIIT IDENTITY paragraph.

## Formation

Γ ⊦ 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ
-------------------- (ty-nu)
Γ ⊦ ν 𝔽₀ ≐ ν 𝔽₁ : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽₀ poly ℓ
Γ ⊦ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ
Γ ⊦ ν 𝔽₀ ≐ ν 𝔽₁ : 𝕌ℓ
-------------------- (ty-nu-inj)
Γ ⊦ 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ

## Elimination

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ t₀ ≐ t₁ : ν 𝔽
----------------------------------- (el-nu-e)
Γ ⊦ out t₀ ≐ out t₁ : ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽)

## Introduction

Γ ⊦ 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌₀
Γ ▷ a ⊦ f₀ ≐ f₁ : ⌊𝔽⌋(a)[↑]
Γ ⊦ t₀ ≐ t₁ : a
------------------------------------------ (el-nu-i)
Γ ⊦ corec 𝔽₀ f₀ t₀ ≐ corec 𝔽₁ f₁ t₁ : ν 𝔽₁

## Computation

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌₀
Γ ▷ a ⊦ f : ⌊𝔽⌋(a)[↑]
Γ ⊦ x : a
--------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-nu-beta)
Γ ⊦ out (corec 𝔽 f x) ≐ map_𝔽 (λ (corec 𝔽[↑] f[↑ ▷ a] ☐₀)) (f[id, x]) : ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽)

## Uniqueness

// (η) — the coinduction principle, el-quot-eta's shape:
// any candidate commuting with the observation IS the corecursor.

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌₀
Γ ▷ a ⊦ f : ⌊𝔽⌋(a)[↑]
Γ ▷ a ⊦ h : (ν 𝔽)[↑]
Γ ▷ a ⊦ out h ≐ (map_𝔽 (λ h))[↑] f : ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽)[↑]
Γ ⊦ x : a
------------------------------------------------------------- (el-nu-eta)
Γ ⊦ h[id, x] ≐ corec 𝔽 f x : ν 𝔽

// Corollary (two-candidate form, as at ℕ and ⊎): two maps into ν 𝔽
// commuting with out through the same coalgebra are equal — chain
// el-nu-eta through the corecursor they both equal. This is the
// internal BISIMULATION-IMPLIES-EQUALITY principle: a bisimulation
// is a coalgebra on its own carrier, and its two projections
// commute.

## Coinduction, relational form

// el-nu-eta's corollary adopted as a
// rule for the kernel's convenience (the el-squash-e-eq precedent:
// ADMISSIBLE, kept because the kernel checks it directly). It needs
// THE RELATOR lift_𝔽(R) — the relation lifting of a polynomial, for a
// relation R on a code c, a function term into Ω. Its β-equations
// follow the shape of 𝔽: the sum by ⊎-elim at motive Ω, ⊥ = ∥𝟘∥ off
// the diagonal (the tag mismatch judgementally visible); at a
// dependent pair the second components are compared under the
// equation of the first, where their types agree by el-reflect — no
// transport, the same extensional degeneration as the QIIT ᴰ-clauses.

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ c : 𝕌ℓ      Γ ▷ c ▷ c[↑] ⊦ R : Ω
------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-relator)
Γ ⊦ lift_𝔽(R) : ⌊𝔽⌋(c) → ⌊𝔽⌋(c)[↑] → Ω

Γ ⊦ lift_𝕏(R) : ⌊𝕏⌋(c) → ⌊𝕏⌋(c)[↑] → Ω      Γ ⊦ u : c      Γ ⊦ v : c
------------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-relator-hole)
Γ ⊦ lift_𝕏(R) u v ≐ R[id, u, v] : Ω

Γ ⊦ lift_{K a}(R) : ⌊K a⌋(c) → ⌊K a⌋(c)[↑] → Ω      Γ ⊦ u : a      Γ ⊦ v : a
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-relator-const)
Γ ⊦ lift_{K a}(R) u v ≐ (u ≡ v ∈ a) : Ω

Γ ⊦ lift_{𝔽 × 𝔾}(R) : ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c) → ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c)[↑] → Ω      Γ ⊦ u : ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c)      Γ ⊦ v : ⌊𝔽 × 𝔾⌋(c)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-relator-prod)
Γ ⊦ lift_{𝔽 × 𝔾}(R) u v ≐ ∥lift_𝔽(R) (u .π₁) (v .π₁) × (lift_𝔾(R) (u .π₂) (v .π₂))[↑]∥ : Ω

Γ ⊦ lift_{𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾}(R) : ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c) → ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c)[↑] → Ω      Γ ⊦ u : ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c)      Γ ⊦ v : ⌊𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾⌋(c)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-relator-sum)
Γ ⊦ lift_{𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾}(R) u v ≐ ⊎-elim (⊎-elim (lift_𝔽(R)[↑ ∘ ↑] ☐₁ ☐₀) ∥𝟘∥ v[↑]) (⊎-elim ∥𝟘∥ (lift_𝔾(R)[↑ ∘ ↑] ☐₁ ☐₀) v[↑]) u : Ω

Γ ⊦ lift_{a × 𝔽}(R) : ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c) → ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c)[↑] → Ω      Γ ⊦ u : ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c)      Γ ⊦ v : ⌊a × 𝔽⌋(c)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-relator-sigma)
Γ ⊦ lift_{a × 𝔽}(R) u v ≐ ∥(u .π₁ ≡ v .π₁ ∈ a) × lift_{𝔽[id, u .π₁]}(R)[↑] (u[↑] .π₂) (v[↑] .π₂)∥ : Ω

Γ ⊦ lift_{a → 𝔽}(R) : ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c) → ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c)[↑] → Ω      Γ ⊦ u : ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c)      Γ ⊦ v : ⌊a → 𝔽⌋(c)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-relator-pi)
Γ ⊦ lift_{a → 𝔽}(R) u v ≐ ∥a → lift_𝔽(R[↑ ▷ c ▷ c[↑]]) (u[↑] ☐₀) (v[↑] ☐₀)∥ : Ω

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ
Γ ▷ ν 𝔽 ▷ (ν 𝔽)[↑] ⊦ R : Ω
Γ ⊦ p : R[id, t₀, t₁]
Γ ▷ ν 𝔽 ▷ (ν 𝔽)[↑] ▷ R ⊦ q : lift_𝔽(R)[↑ ∘ ↑ ∘ ↑] (out ☐₂) (out ☐₁)
Γ ⊦ t₀ : ν 𝔽      Γ ⊦ t₁ : ν 𝔽
------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-nu-coind)
Γ ⊦ t₀ ≐ t₁ : ν 𝔽

## Derivation

// (why admissible). From R build the subset carrier
// b ≔ (νᶜ × νᶜ) × prf R — νᶜ the ν-code, prf the derivable prf-code
// of the Ω block's impredicativity note — with the coalgebra
// observing the FIRST component, the closure q transporting the
// invariant to the tails; both projections commute with out (the
// second by q's head equations, reflected), so el-nu-eta equates
// them through the corecursor, and instantiating at (t₀, t₁, p)
// gives the conclusion. The kernel checks the rule as stated
// instead: the subset-carrier construction is the JUSTIFICATION, not
// the implementation.

## Substitution action

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
-------------------------- (poly-sub)
Θ ⊦ 𝔽[σ] poly ℓ

σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
--------------------- (poly-sub-hole)
Θ ⊦ 𝕏[σ] ≐ 𝕏 poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ a : 𝕌ℓ      σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
---------------------------- (poly-sub-const)
Θ ⊦ (K a)[σ] ≐ K a[σ] poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 × 𝔾 poly ℓ      σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
---------------------------------- (poly-sub-prod)
Θ ⊦ (𝔽 × 𝔾)[σ] ≐ 𝔽[σ] × 𝔾[σ] poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾 poly ℓ      σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
---------------------------------- (poly-sub-sum)
Θ ⊦ (𝔽 ⊎ 𝔾)[σ] ≐ 𝔽[σ] ⊎ 𝔾[σ] poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ a × 𝔽 poly ℓ      σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
------------------------------------ (poly-sub-sigma)
Θ ⊦ (a × 𝔽)[σ] ≐ a[σ] × 𝔽[σ ▷ a] poly ℓ

Γ ⊦ a → 𝔽 poly ℓ      σ : Θ ⇒ Γ
--------------------------------------- (poly-sub-pi)
Θ ⊦ (a → 𝔽)[σ] ≐ a[σ] → 𝔽[σ ▷ a] poly ℓ

Γ₁ ⊦ ν 𝔽 : 𝕌ℓ      σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------- (ty-sub-nu)
Γ₀ ⊦ (ν 𝔽)[σ] ≐ ν 𝔽[σ] : 𝕌ℓ

Γ₁ ⊦ out t : A      σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
--------------------------------- (el-sub-nu-e)
Γ₀ ⊦ (out t)[σ] ≐ out t[σ] : A[σ]

Γ₁ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ₁ ⊦ a : 𝕌₀      Γ₁ ▷ a ⊦ f : ⌊𝔽⌋(a)[↑]      Γ₁ ⊦ x : a      σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-sub-nu-i)
Γ₀ ⊦ (corec 𝔽 f x)[σ] ≐ corec 𝔽[σ] f[σ ▷ a] x[σ] : (ν 𝔽)[σ]

## Notes

//   * LAMBEK. in ≔ λ (corec 𝔽 (map_𝔽 (λ (out ☐₀)) ☐₀) ☐₀), at the
//     carrier ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽), inverts out
//     up to ≐ — out ∘ in by el-nu-beta plus the functor laws,
//     in ∘ out by el-nu-eta — so ν 𝔽 ≅ ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽) elementwise,
//     while the TYPES stay structurally distinct (IDENTITY above).
//   * SUBSUMPTION (conservativity). Every ν 𝔽 is definable: with
//     F̂ⁿ(𝟙) : 𝕌ℓ by ℕ-elim at motive 𝕌ℓ (a 𝕌ℓ₊₁ family), the ℕ-indexed limit
//         (g : ℕ → (F̂ⁿ 𝟙)-family) × (restriction coherence)
//     is a final 𝔽-coalgebra — containers preserve this limit — with
//     out, corec and both laws provable (β up to lemmas, η by
//     ℕ-induction and funext-via-reflection). The scheme is retained
//     for structural identity, one-step β, and the uniform η; the
//     encoding is its justification, exactly as the QIIT SEMANTICS
//     note is for that scheme.
//   * SEMANTICS. In the setoid model the carrier of ν 𝔽 is the
//     meta-level limit above (the descending chain of the monotone
//     operator, converging at ω), and the relation is the LARGEST
//     BISIMULATION — el-nu-eta is finality, validated on the nose.
//     Models that fail finality are hereby excluded, as models
//     failing initiality are by the QIIT notes.
//   * DELIBERATE OMISSIONS, each with a known upgrade path: no
//     internal fixpoints in the grammar (interleaved nesting like
//     ν of X ↦ A × List X needs the inner functor reified to
//     shape-and-positions form by hand; non-interleaved nesting is
//     free through K-constants at previously formed ν/QIIT codes);
//     no indexed or mutual coinductive sorts and no coequations
//     (those want the full dual theory of cosignatures); no ν under
//     a QIIT constructor domain (an inner ν forces infinitary
//     branching, which the finitary ToS grammar excludes).
//
// EXAMPLES.
//     Stream a  ≔ ν (K a × 𝕏)
//     Conat     ≔ ν (K 𝟙 ⊎ 𝕏)
//     Colist a  ≔ ν (K 𝟙 ⊎ (K a × 𝕏))
//     Cotree a  ≔ ν (K 𝟙 ⊎ (K a × (𝕏 × 𝕏)))    # leaf/node infinite trees
//     Moore a b ≔ ν (K b × (a → 𝕏))
//   head, tail, and friends are out followed by projections and
//   ⊎-elim; constructors (cons, and Cotree's leaf/node) are in
//   instances. Surface codata declarations elaborate to
//   ν-polynomials — the elaborator's business.

# Rules (elem list)

Γ ctx
------------- (sp-empty)
Γ ⊦ · : ε

Γ ▷ A ⊦ Δ tel
Γ ⊦ e₀ ≐ e₁ : A
Γ ⊦ ē₀ ≐ ē₁ : Δ[id, e₁]
--------------------------------- (sp-ext)        // defining clause of the
Γ ⊦ (e₀, ē₀) ≐ (e₁, ē₁) : A ◁ Δ                   //   pointwise equation

Γ₁ ⊦ ē₀ ≐ ē₁ : Δ
σ₀ ≐ σ₁ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
----------------------------------- (sp-sub) // the action: sp-sub-empty, sp-sub-ext
Γ₀ ⊦ ē₀[σ₀] ≐ ē₁[σ₁] : Δ[σ₁]

σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
----------------------- (sp-sub-empty)
Γ₀ ⊦ ·[σ] ≐ · : ε

Γ₁ ⊦ e : A
Γ₁ ▷ A ⊦ Δ tel
Γ₁ ⊦ ē : Δ[id, e]
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------------------ (sp-sub-ext)
Γ₀ ⊦ (e, ē)[σ] ≐ e[σ], ē[σ] : A[σ] ◁ Δ[σ ▷ A]

Γ ⊦ ē : Δ
------------------------ (sp-eta)   // admissible: a spine is the spine of its
Γ ⊦ ē ≐ ☐(Δ)[id, ē] : Δ            //   components — by induction on the
                                   //   derivation; at 𝒮-elim, el-qiit-eta

Γ ≐ Γ' ctx
Γ ⊦ ē : Δ
--------------- (sp-coe-ctx)
Γ' ⊦ ē : Δ

Γ ⊦ Δ ≐ Δ' tel
Γ ⊦ ē : Δ
------------------ (sp-coe-tel)
Γ ⊦ ē : Δ'

Γ ≐ Γ' ctx
Γ ⊦ ē ≐ ē' : Δ
-------------------- (sp-eq-coe-ctx)
Γ' ⊦ ē ≐ ē' : Δ

Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel
Γ ⊦ ē₀ ≐ ē₁ : Δ₀
-------------------- (sp-eq-coe-tel)
Γ ⊦ ē₀ ≐ ē₁ : Δ₁

# Record types (labelled telescopes)

// Rec l̄ Δ is a telescope Δ with a label per entry. The labels are a
// parallel list — Δ stays an ordinary nameless telescope, so a label
// never binds and the tel-/sp- machinery is reused as is.

// SIDE CONDITIONS on label lists — meta-level, context-free.

· distinct

l̄ distinct
l ∉ l̄
------------
l l̄ distinct

// |l̄| = |Δ|: the lists have the same length

## Fields

// Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ: the fields l̄ of t have the types Δ — a SUFFIX of t's
// record, over Γ, the earlier fields instantiated at t's projections.
// A projection and the spine of projections t.l̄ are typed by it.

Γ ⊦ t : Rec l̄ Δ
---------------- (rec-fields)
Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ

Γ ⊦ t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ
----------------------- (rec-fields-step)
Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ[id, t.l]

Γ ⊦ t₀ ≐ t₁ : Rec l̄′ Δ′      Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel      Γ ⊦ t₀ / l̄ ↪ Δ₀
----------------------------------------------------------------- (rec-fields-coe)
Γ ⊦ t₁ / l̄ ↪ Δ₁

Γ ⊦ t / l̄ ↪ Δ
--------------- (sp-rec-proj)
Γ ⊦ t.l̄ : Δ

Γ ⊦ t / · ↪ ε
----------------- (sp-rec-proj-empty)
Γ ⊦ t.· ≐ · : ε

Γ ⊦ t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ
--------------------------------- (sp-rec-proj-ext)
Γ ⊦ t.(l l̄) ≐ t.l, t.l̄ : A ◁ Δ

## Rules

// Γ ⊦ ē : Δ gives Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ at some ℓ (existence); Γ ⊦ t : Rec l̄ Δ
// gives Δ at a level, l̄ distinct and |l̄| = |Δ| by inversion.

Γ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
------------------ (ty-rec)
Γ ⊦ Rec l̄ Δ : 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ ē : Δ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
----------------------- (el-rec-i)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩ : Rec l̄ Δ

Γ ⊦ t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ
-------------------- (el-rec-e)   // congruence: at t₀, then rec-fields-coe
Γ ⊦ t.l : A

// Computation: by the position of the label. The premises are
// el-rec-i's — the components typed, as in el-sigma-beta₁/₂ — not the
// typing of the record: that a typed record has typed components is no
// lemma of the theory, and the rule must not assert it. The miss step
// is well-typed by induction along l̄: the fields of the two records
// agree at the earlier labels by this rule.

Γ ⊦ e, ē : A ◁ Δ
l l̄ distinct
|l l̄| = |A ◁ Δ|
---------------------------- (el-rec-beta)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l l̄ ↪ e, ē⟩.l ≐ e : A

Γ ⊦ e, ē : A ◁ Δ
l′ l̄ distinct
|l′ l̄| = |A ◁ Δ|
Γ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩.l : B
--------------------------------------- (el-rec-beta-miss)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l′ l̄ ↪ e, ē⟩.l ≐ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩.l : B

// Uniqueness, in el-sigma-eta's form and orientation. At l̄ = · this is
// ⟨⟩ ≐ t : Rec · ε — the empty record is a unit type.

Γ ⊦ t : Rec l̄ Δ
---------------------------- (el-rec-eta)
Γ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ t.l̄⟩ ≐ t : Rec l̄ Δ

// Injectivity, at ONE label list: labels are syntax and compare
// syntactically. That records with different label lists are different
// types is no-confusion — like Π against Σ, not a rule, and a
// meta-property of consistent contexts only.

Γ ⊦ Δ₀ tel ℓ
Γ ⊦ Δ₁ tel ℓ
Γ ⊦ Rec l̄ Δ₀ ≐ Rec l̄ Δ₁ : 𝕌ℓ
------------------------------ (ty-rec-inj)
Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel ℓ

// Substitution action.

Γ₁ ⊦ Δ tel ℓ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------ (ty-sub-rec)
Γ₀ ⊦ (Rec l̄ Δ)[σ] ≐ Rec l̄ Δ[σ] : 𝕌ℓ

Γ₁ ⊦ ē : Δ
l̄ distinct
|l̄| = |Δ|
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------------------- (el-sub-record)
Γ₀ ⊦ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩[σ] ≐ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē[σ]⟩ : Rec l̄ Δ[σ]

Γ₁ ⊦ t.l : A
σ : Γ₀ ⇒ Γ₁
------------------------------- (el-sub-rec-proj)
Γ₀ ⊦ (t.l)[σ] ≐ t[σ].l : A[σ]
